window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"t":"Decision records","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html","k":"Each ADR records a decision that is expensive to reverse: why it was made, what it costs, and what would make us revisit it. Never edit an accepted ADR. Supersede it with a new one."},{"t":"Index","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#index","k":"ADR Title Status 001 Modular monolith with Spring Modulith Accepted 002 Local-first register with SQLite Accepted 003 One React register UI in Electron and Capacitor shells Accepted 004 Shared-schema multi-tenancy with r"},{"t":"Records","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#records","k":""},{"t":"ADR-001 · Modular monolith with Spring Modulith","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-001","k":"Context. One engineer, one database, and sales and stock must change together atomically. Microservices would add network failures, distributed transactions and operational cost with no benefit at this scale. Decision. O"},{"t":"ADR-002 · Local-first register with SQLite","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-002","k":"Context. Sri Lankan shops have unreliable internet and power. Competitors sell offline billing. The original blueprint deferred offline to V1.2, which would have forced a rewrite of checkout, numbering and stock rules. D"},{"t":"ADR-003 · One React register UI in Electron and Capacitor shells","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-003","k":"Context. Counters use Windows PCs and Android tablets. The team is one engineer who knows React and TypeScript. Decision. One React app and one pure-TypeScript domain package. Electron packages it for Windows and Capacit"},{"t":"ADR-004 · Shared-schema multi-tenancy with row-level security","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-004","k":"Context. Hundreds of small tenants, low cost per tenant, one team. Decision. One database and schema. tenant_id on every tenant-owned table. PostgreSQL RLS forced on these tables, with the tenant set per transaction. Con"},{"t":"ADR-005 · Stock as an append-only movement ledger with batch-level FEFO","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-005","k":"Decision. All stock changes are stock_movement rows at batch level. stock_balance is a projection updated in the same transaction and checked nightly. Allocation is FEFO unless the cashier or a GS1 code names a batch. Co"},{"t":"ADR-006 · Industry features as extension modules","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-006","k":"Context. Retail, pharmacy and grocery now; restaurant and salon later. Putting industry logic in Sales would make the core unmaintainable. Decision. The core understands a generic sale. Industry modules implement named S"},{"t":"ADR-007 · Transactional outbox via event publication registry, no broker","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-007","k":"Decision. Domain events are stored in the same transaction (Spring Modulith event publication registry) and delivered to in-process listeners, with retries for incomplete publications. No Kafka or RabbitMQ. Consequences."},{"t":"ADR-008 · Stay out of PCI-DSS scope","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-008","k":"Decision. Card data never enters RetailOS. MVP: standalone terminals, recording the approval reference only. R3: semi-integrated terminals that return only the result. Consequences. No PCI audit cost. Slightly slower car"},{"t":"ADR-009 · Cloud-agnostic container hosting, no Kubernetes","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-009","k":"Decision. One OCI image, PostgreSQL and S3-compatible storage. It runs on a VPS with Docker Compose at pilot stage, and on any managed container service later. Configuration via env vars, with an off-site backup at a sec"},{"t":"ADR-010 · Sales are never rejected; exceptions instead","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-010","k":"Context. A sale made offline has already happened: the customer has left with the goods. The server can't undo it. Decision. The server records every completed sale. Price mismatches, short stock, expired batches and clo"},{"t":"ADR-011 · Register-generated UUIDv7 and per-register receipt sequences","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-011","k":"Decision. Registers create IDs (UUIDv7) for every fact they create, and number receipts from their own gap-free sequence. The server enforces uniqueness through sync_inbox and receipt_registry . Consequences. No coordina"},{"t":"ADR-012 · Shared test vectors for logic duplicated in Java and TypeScript","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-012","k":"Context. Pricing, tax, rounding, GS1 parsing and promotions run on the register (offline) and are checked on the server. Decision. Keep the logic in both languages, but drive both test suites from the same JSON vectors i"},{"t":"ADR-013 · Sinhala and Tamil receipts printed as raster images","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-013","k":"Context. Most thermal printers don't have Sinhala or Tamil fonts, and complex script shaping isn't supported in ESC/POS text mode. Decision. The register renders the receipt (or the non-Latin parts) to a 1-bit image with"},{"t":"ADR-014 · JPA for CRUD, explicit SQL for stock and reports","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#adr-014","k":"Decision. Spring Data JPA for master data and admin CRUD. JdbcClient with hand-written SQL for allocation, row locking, ledger checks and reports, where you need to see the exact query. Consequences. Two data-access styl"},{"t":"ADR template","p":"Decision records","u":"adr.html#template","k":"### ADR-0NN · Title Status: Proposed | Accepted | Superseded by ADR-0MM Date: YYYY-MM-DD Context: what forces are at play (constraints, requirements IDs, metrics) Decision: what we will do, stated plainly Consequences: w"},{"t":"Guide for AI agents","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html","k":"This page is written for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor and similar) and for humans who direct them. It is the most compact statement of how RetailOS must behave. A plain-text copy is in ai/AGENTS.md and "},{"t":"Invariants (canonical list)","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#invariants","k":"These rules are never broken. Cite the ID in code comments next to the code that enforces it, and in test names. ID Invariant Enforced by INV-01 Every tenant-owned row has tenant_id . Every DB transaction sets app.tenant"},{"t":"Where things live","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#file-map","k":"Task touches… Look in Read first Checkout, cart, discounts on the register packages/register-core/src/cart , apps/register/src/screens/checkout Sale lifecycle , BR-01..BR-04 Tax calculation backend/…/tax , packages/regis"},{"t":"Rules for agents","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#do-dont","k":"Always Run the module's tests plus ModularityTest before declaring done. Add tenant_id + RLS + an isolation test for every new table. Use the shared Money / Decimal types. Write expand-only migrations, one concern per fi"},{"t":"Task recipes (prompts that work)","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#recipes","k":"Implement a feature from the catalogue Read Doc/ai/AGENTS.md, Doc/requirements.html (F-xxx and related BR-xx), and the module section in Doc/modules.html. Propose the change as: 1) schema migration, 2) domain + tests, 3)"},{"t":"How an agent proves its work","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#verify","k":"./backend/gradlew -p backend test # unit + module + Testcontainers ./backend/gradlew -p backend modulithVerify # boundaries pnpm -r test # register-core, admin, register pnpm -r lint && pnpm i18n:check # lint, money rule"},{"t":"Machine-readable files in this folder","p":"Guide for AI agents","u":"ai-guide.html#machine-files","k":"File Use llms.txt Index of every page with a one-line summary, following the llms.txt convention ai/AGENTS.md Drop-in agent instructions for the repository root ai/system-context.md Condensed system description (architec"},{"t":"API design","p":"API design","u":"api.html","k":"There are two APIs on one backend. The REST API ( /api/v1 ) is for the admin web and online register lookups. The Sync API ( /sync/v1 ) is for register pull and push. Both are described in one OpenAPI document, and the T"},{"t":"Conventions","p":"API design","u":"api.html#conventions","k":"Topic Rule Style Resource-oriented REST, JSON, camelCase fields, plural nouns: /api/v1/products/{id} . Actions that aren't CRUD use a verb sub-resource: POST /api/v1/cash-sessions/{id}/close . Versioning Major version in"},{"t":"Standard headers","p":"API design","u":"api.html#headers","k":"Header Who sends Purpose Authorization: Bearer … All clients JWT access token (10 min). Tenant and user are taken from the token, never from the body. X-Device-Id Registers Enrolled device. Must match the device bound to"},{"t":"Error format","p":"API design","u":"api.html#errors","k":"Errors use RFC 9457 Problem Details with a stable code (see the error code catalog ). HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden Content-Type: application/problem+json { \"type\": \"urn:retailos:error:AUTH-003\", \"title\": \"Permission denied\", \""},{"t":"Endpoint catalog (MVP)","p":"API design","u":"api.html#catalog","k":""},{"t":"Auth and devices","p":"API design","u":"api.html#ep-auth","k":"Method Path Purpose Permission POST /api/v1/auth/login E-mail + password (+ TOTP) → access + refresh token public, rate limited POST /api/v1/auth/refresh Rotate refresh token refresh token POST /api/v1/auth/logout Revoke"},{"t":"Sync","p":"API design","u":"api.html#ep-sync","k":"Method Path Purpose GET /sync/v1/snapshot?scope=catalog Returns a signed URL for the latest snapshot file and its cursor GET /sync/v1/changes?scopes=…&cursor=… Change feed (pull) POST /sync/v1/push Batch of facts: sales,"},{"t":"Catalog, pricing, inventory","p":"API design","u":"api.html#ep-catalog","k":"Method Path Purpose GET/POST /api/v1/products List and search, create GET/PUT /api/v1/products/{id} Read, update (If-Match) POST /api/v1/products/{id}/skus Add variant GET /api/v1/barcodes/{code} Resolve barcode (online "},{"t":"Sales, cash, customers, tax","p":"API design","u":"api.html#ep-sales","k":"Method Path Purpose GET /api/v1/sales?branchId=&from=&to= Sales history GET /api/v1/sales/{id} , /sales/by-receipt/{receiptNo} Sale detail, lookup for returns GET /api/v1/sale-exceptions?status=OPEN Exception queue (nega"},{"t":"Tenant administration","p":"API design","u":"api.html#ep-admin","k":"Method Path Purpose GET/PUT /api/v1/tenant , /tenant/settings Business profile, VAT number, receipt options GET/POST /api/v1/branches , /branches/{id}/registers Branches and registers GET/POST /api/v1/users , /roles User"},{"t":"Rate limits","p":"API design","u":"api.html#rate-limits","k":"Endpoint group Limit Key Login, PIN, enroll, refresh 10 per minute, then exponential lockout IP + account / device REST (admin) 300 per minute user Sync pull 120 per minute device Sync push 60 per minute (50 items each) "},{"t":"OpenAPI and client generation","p":"API design","u":"api.html#openapi","k":"springdoc generates /v3/api-docs , and CI saves it as backend/openapi.json . A diff check fails the build on breaking changes ( openapi-diff ). packages/api-client is generated with openapi-typescript and openapi-fetch ."},{"t":"System architecture","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html","k":"RetailOS has three deployable parts: a modular monolith backend, an admin web app, and a register app packaged for Windows and Android. This page shows how they fit together, from the outside in, following the C4 model."},{"t":"Architecture principles","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#principles","k":"# Principle What it means in practice P1 The till never stops Anything a cashier does works offline. The network is for syncing, not for selling. P2 Facts are immutable Sales, payments, stock movements and audit entries "},{"t":"Level 1: system context","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#context","k":"Dashed lines are external integrations behind adapters. They are optional and released later."},{"t":"Level 2: containers","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#containers","k":"Backend and worker run the same container image with different Spring profiles. In the MVP they can run as one process. Container Responsibility Technology Scales by Register app Checkout, returns, shift, receiving at th"},{"t":"Inside the register app","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#register","k":"The register is where most of the complexity sits, because it must behave correctly with no server. It is built in layers so the business logic is shared by both shells and can be tested in plain Node. Business rules liv"},{"t":"Register design rules","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#register-rules","k":"register-core has no React, DOM, Electron or Capacitor imports. It runs under Vitest in Node. Ports are TypeScript interfaces: LocalStore , DeviceBridge , Clock , IdGenerator , SyncTransport . Each shell provides adapter"},{"t":"Inside the backend","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#backend","k":"One Spring Boot application, split into modules under com.devcity.retailos.<module> . Spring Modulith checks in CI that no module reaches into another's internals ( INV-08 ). Solid arrows are synchronous calls to a modul"},{"t":"Layers inside a module","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#layers","k":"Complex modules (sales, inventory, pricing, tax, sync) use a light hexagonal layout. Simple CRUD modules use controller → service → repository. Don't force four layers on a categories table. sales/ ├─ SalesApi.java ← pub"},{"t":"Quality attribute strategies","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#quality","k":"Quality Strategy Where Scalability Registers do the CPU work, so the server only ingests facts. The backend is stateless and scales horizontally. Large fact tables are partitioned by month, reports run on a read replica,"},{"t":"How the architecture evolves","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#evolution","k":"Each step has a trigger metric. See Cost & scaling ."},{"t":"Repository layout","p":"System architecture","u":"architecture.html#repo","k":"One monorepo, so one developer (or an AI agent) can change the API, the register and the docs in a single commit. retailos/ ├─ backend/ Spring Boot app (Gradle) │ ├─ src/main/java/com/devcity/retailos/{platform,catalog,p"},{"t":"Cost & scaling","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html","k":"The architecture is cheap to run by design: registers do the heavy work, so the server mostly stores facts. One process and one database carry the product a long way. Spend more only when a measured trigger says so. Pric"},{"t":"Cost principles","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#principles","k":"Push work to the edge. Pricing, tax, search and receipts run on the shop's own hardware. The cloud only ingests facts and serves changes. One image, one database. No Kubernetes, Kafka, Redis or separate search cluster un"},{"t":"Workload sizing","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#sizing","k":"Assumptions for a typical branch: 2 registers, 400 sales a day, 4 lines per sale, 12 trading hours, with the busiest hour carrying 15% of the day. Quantity Per branch 100 branches 1,000 branches Sales per day 400 40,000 "},{"t":"Monthly cost by stage (indicative)","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#stages","k":"Item Stage 1: pilot (≤ 20 branches) Stage 2: growth (≤ 300 branches) Stage 3: scale (≤ 2,000 branches) App compute 1 VM, 2 vCPU / 4 GB: $12–25 2–3 instances, 2 vCPU / 4 GB: $40–90 3–6 instances (autoscale): $150–350 Post"},{"t":"Cost levers","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#levers","k":"Lever Saves How Delta sync + gzip + snapshots on CDN Egress, CPU Registers download only changes. Full catalogs come from cached static files. ARM instances ~20–40% compute Java 25 and PostgreSQL run well on ARM. Build m"},{"t":"Cost traps to avoid","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#traps","k":"Managed NAT gateways on some clouds cost a fixed hourly fee plus per-GB charges, often more than the app server itself. Use public subnets with tight security groups, or provider setups without NAT, at Stage 1–2. Kuberne"},{"t":"Tracking cost per tenant","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#monitoring-cost","k":"Every month, a worker job records per tenant: sales count, rows written, storage used (partition sizes by tenant are estimated from row counts), sync bytes, messages sent, support tickets. Tenant cost = shared infrastruc"},{"t":"Scaling path and triggers","p":"Cost & scaling","u":"cost.html#scaling","k":"Step Do it when (trigger) What changes 1. Separate DB from app host DB CPU or memory competes with the app; > 20 branches; or before the first paying contract Managed PostgreSQL with PITR 2. Second app instance Need zero"},{"t":"Data model","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html","k":"PostgreSQL is the system of record for every tenant. The model has four areas: organisation, catalog and pricing, inventory and purchasing, and sales and money. Fact tables are append-only. Balances are projections that "},{"t":"Conventions","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#conventions","k":"Topic Rule Primary keys uuid , version 7 (time-ordered, so indexes stay compact). Created by the server with uuidv7() , or by the register for facts it creates ( INV-05 ). Tenant Every tenant-owned table has tenant_id uu"},{"t":"Organisation, identity and devices","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#erd-org","k":"Tenant → branch → register is in the schema from day one, even for single-shop customers."},{"t":"Catalog and pricing","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#erd-catalog","k":""},{"t":"Inventory and purchasing","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#erd-inventory","k":"stock_movement is the ledger. stock_balance is the projection, rebuilt nightly to detect drift ( INV-04 )."},{"t":"Sales, payments, cash, customers and tax","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#erd-sales","k":""},{"t":"Key table definitions","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#key-tables","k":"These are the authoritative shapes. Flyway migrations must match them. Abbreviated: indexes and audit columns are omitted where obvious. sale and sale_line create table sale ( id uuid not null, -- generated on the regist"},{"t":"Row-level security","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#rls","k":"Tenant isolation is enforced twice. Every repository filters by tenant_id , and PostgreSQL RLS blocks any row of another tenant even when a query forgets the filter. alter table sale enable row level security; alter tabl"},{"t":"Partitioning, indexing, retention","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#partitioning","k":"Table Partitioning Key indexes sale , sale_line , payment Range by business_date , monthly. Partitions created 3 months ahead by a job. (tenant_id, branch_id, business_date) , (tenant_id, receipt_no) , (tenant_id, custom"},{"t":"Register local schema (SQLite)","p":"Data model","u":"data-model.html#local-schema","k":"The register keeps a subset scoped to its branch, plus its own outbox. Table names match the server, so code and people only learn one vocabulary. Group Tables Source Reference data (pulled) product, sku, barcode, unit_c"},{"t":"Deployment & CI/CD","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html","k":"The goal is boring, repeatable releases that one engineer can run on a Friday without fear. Everything is a container image or a signed installer, built by CI, and nothing is deployed from a laptop. The design doesn't de"},{"t":"Environments","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#environments","k":"Environment Purpose Runs on Data local Development docker compose up : PostgreSQL, MinIO (S3), Mailpit, backend with hot reload Seed script with 2 demo tenants (retail + pharmacy) ci Automated tests CI runners + Testcont"},{"t":"CI/CD pipeline","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#pipeline","k":"GitHub Actions is assumed (free tier is enough at the start), but every step is a plain script in infra/ci/ , so moving to another CI is easy."},{"t":"Keeping CI fast and cheap","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#ci-budget","k":"Cache Gradle, pnpm and Docker layers. Run front-end jobs only when apps/ or packages/ change (path filters). Run Testcontainers PostgreSQL once per test JVM with a template database per test class, not a container per te"},{"t":"Production topology by stage","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#topology","k":"Move to the next stage only when its trigger metric is reached. See Cost & scaling ."},{"t":"Hosting options (decide later)","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#hosting-options","k":"Building block Portable requirement Examples Compute Runs an OCI container with env vars and a health check A VPS with Docker Compose, AWS ECS/Fargate or Lightsail, Azure Container Apps, Google Cloud Run, Fly.io, Digital"},{"t":"The backend container","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#container","k":"# backend/Dockerfile (multi-stage) FROM eclipse-temurin:25-jdk AS build WORKDIR /src COPY . . RUN ./gradlew bootJar -x test --no-daemon FROM eclipse-temurin:25-jre-alpine RUN addgroup -S app && adduser -S app -G app WORK"},{"t":"Zero-downtime deploys","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#zero-downtime","k":"CI pushes the signed image retailos:1.6.0 . The migration job runs expand-only migrations (new tables, nullable columns, new indexes created CONCURRENTLY ). The old version keeps working. Rolling restart: start the new i"},{"t":"Database migration rules","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#migrations","k":"Flyway versioned scripts: V2026_11_19_1__add_batch_status.sql . Never edit a script once it's merged. Every migration must be backward compatible with the previous app version (expand/contract). Large backfills run as id"},{"t":"Register app releases","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#releases","k":"Topic Windows (Electron) Android (Capacitor) Packaging NSIS installer via electron-builder, Authenticode code-signed AAB for Play Store (managed Google Play for business), or a signed APK through an MDM Updates electron-"},{"t":"Feature flags","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#flags","k":"Simple database-backed flags ( feature_flag(key, scope global|tenant|register, enabled, rollout_pct) ), synced to registers in the settings scope. Use them to ship unfinished code safely and to enable features for pilot "},{"t":"Versioning","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#versioning","k":"Semantic versioning for backend, admin and register, with one shared version number per release train (e.g. 1.6.0 ), so support knows what goes with what. A changelog is generated from Conventional Commits. Release notes"},{"t":"Backups and disaster recovery","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#backup","k":"What How Retention PostgreSQL Continuous WAL archiving + daily base backup (managed PITR, or WAL-G/pgBackRest to a bucket). RPO ≤ 5 min. PITR 14 days, daily 35 days, monthly 12 months Off-site copy Encrypted daily logica"},{"t":"Disaster scenarios","p":"Deployment & CI/CD","u":"deployment.html#dr","k":"Scenario Impact on shops Recovery App host down None for selling. Admin web unavailable. Redeploy the image on any host (same env vars). Target under 30 min. Database lost or corrupted None for selling. Registers queue. "},{"t":"Developer guide","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html","k":"Everything a new developer needs on day one, and what everyone follows every day after. If this page and the code disagree, fix one of them in the same pull request."},{"t":"Day one","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#day-one","k":"Read the Overview , the Glossary and the invariants . Set up the local stack (below) and run all tests. Walk through one sale: scan → complete → sync → server allocation → report, using Offline & sync and Key flows next "},{"t":"Local setup","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#setup","k":"Prerequisites: Git, Docker Desktop, JDK 25 (Temurin), Node 22 LTS + pnpm 9, an IDE (IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code). Optional: an 80 mm ESC/POS printer or a network printer emulator. git clone <repo-url> retailos && cd retailo"},{"t":"Java conventions (backend)","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#java","k":"Package by module: com.devcity.retailos.<module> . Only the module root, events and spi packages are public. Everything else lives in internal . Domain classes have no Spring or JPA annotations in rich modules. Map to pe"},{"t":"TypeScript conventions (admin and register)","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#ts","k":"strict: true , no any (lint error), and zod schemas at the edges (API responses, local DB rows). Money and quantity use Decimal from decimal.js , serialised as strings. A lint rule flags arithmetic on money fields. regis"},{"t":"Testing strategy","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#testing","k":"Must-have test Proves TenantIsolationIT No cross-tenant reads through any repository or endpoint ( INV-01 ) ModularityTest Module boundaries hold ( INV-08 ) SyncIdempotencyIT Pushing the same sale 3 times records it once"},{"t":"Git workflow","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#git","k":"Trunk-based: short-lived branches feat/… , fix/… , merged to main by PR within a few days. Unfinished work goes behind a feature flag. Conventional Commits: feat(sales): record batch hint from GS1 scan . These generate t"},{"t":"Definition of done","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#dod","k":"Acceptance criteria from the user story pass as automated tests. Works offline on the register (if it's a register feature) and survives an app restart. Strings translated to si/ta (machine draft allowed, marked for revi"},{"t":"Walkthrough: adding a feature end to end","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#add-feature","k":"Example: F-209 near-expiry discount suggestion . Spec: add acceptance criteria to the requirement (or ticket). Decide which module owns it: inventory (expiry) + pricing (suggestion). Schema: V2027_02_10_1__near_expiry_ru"},{"t":"Debugging locally","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#debugging","k":"Backend: run with the local profile for SQL logging ( logging.level.org.springframework.jdbc.core=DEBUG and Hibernate SQL). The Actuator endpoint /actuator/modulith lists modules and events. Register: Ctrl+Shift+D opens "},{"t":"Code review checklist","p":"Developer guide","u":"dev-guide.html#review","k":"Which invariants does this touch? Are they tested? Does any module read another module's table or internal class? Money: decimals only, rounding as BR-03? Can this fail offline? What does the cashier see? Is it safe to r"},{"t":"Industry extensions","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html","k":"The core POS understands a generic sale. Industry modules add workflows and data through a small set of named extension points. A tenant switches modules on, and the core never imports an extension."},{"t":"What is core and what is an extension","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#core-vs-ext","k":"Several features that look industry-specific are needed by more than one industry, so they belong in the core. Capability Lives in Why Batches, expiry, FEFO Core (inventory) Pharmacies, supermarkets and FMCG all need it."},{"t":"How extensions plug in","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#mechanism","k":"The same switch (tenant_module) controls server SPIs, register plugins and which extension data is synced."},{"t":"Server extension points (SPI)","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#spi","k":"Each SPI is a Java interface in the core module's spi package. Extensions implement it as a Spring bean annotated with the module key. The core asks ExtensionRegistry for implementations enabled for the current tenant. /"},{"t":"Register plugins","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#register-plugins","k":"Register plugins are bundled into the app at build time, not downloaded at runtime: that is safer and works offline. They are activated by the tenant's enabled modules. // packages/register-core/src/extensions/types.ts e"},{"t":"Data ownership rules","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#data-rules","k":"Extensions own tables with a prefix ( ph_ , gr_ , rs_ , sl_ ) and reference core rows by ID. Never add industry columns to core tables. Core tables have one attributes jsonb column for display-only extras. Anything you f"},{"t":"Enablement and licensing","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#enablement","k":"tenant_module (tenant_id, module_key, enabled, plan, enabled_at, settings jsonb) -- e.g. ('t1', 'pharmacy', true, 'PRO', ..., '{\"requireRxForScheduleB\": true}') This table doubles as the billing entitlement: industry mod"},{"t":"Pharmacy module R2","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#pharmacy","k":"Feature Design Drug information ph_drug_info(sku_id, generic_name, strength, form, schedule_class, prescription_required, manufacturer) . Generic-name search is in the MVP core search index. Generic substitution Search b"},{"t":"Grocery module R2","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#grocery","k":"Feature Design PLU codes gr_plu(plu_code, sku_id, tare_g, price_mode) , used by the scale and the barcode parser. Scale barcode profiles gr_scale_profile(prefix, plu_digits, value_digits, value_type WEIGHT|PRICE, decimal"},{"t":"Restaurant module Later","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#restaurant","k":"Uses the core OPEN sale state as a running ticket: lines are added over time and the ticket is completed at payment. rs_table , rs_floor , rs_ticket(sale_id, table_id, covers, server_id) , rs_kot(id, ticket_id, station, "},{"t":"Salon module Later","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#salon","k":"sl_appointment(id, customer_id, staff_id, service_sku_id, starts_at, ends_at, status) and sl_staff_schedule . Checking in an appointment creates an OPEN sale with SERVICE lines and staff_id set. Commission reports read t"},{"t":"Checklist: adding a new industry module","p":"Industry extensions","u":"extensions.html#add-extension","k":"Write an ADR: what the module does and which existing SPIs it uses. If it needs a new SPI, justify it with at least one concrete use case. Create the ext.<key> package with internal/ , its own Flyway location and a table"},{"t":"Key flows","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html","k":"The flows below are the ones developers must get exactly right. Each one lists the invariants it protects. The register-side sale and sync flow is on Offline & sync ."},{"t":"Sale lifecycle","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#sale-states","k":"COMPLETED is final for the sale record itself ( INV-02 ). Return states are derived from linked return records, not by editing the sale."},{"t":"Server: recording a synced sale","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#record-sale","k":"Protects INV-02 INV-04 INV-05 INV-07 INV-14 ."},{"t":"FEFO allocation algorithm","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#fefo","k":"allocate(line, location): need = line.base_qty if line.batch_hint is set: # cashier picked it or GS1 scan carried it take min(need, onHand(hint)) from hint, or all of need if hint is the only batch need -= taken candidat"},{"t":"Goods receiving with GS1 2D","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#receiving","k":"GS1 Application Identifiers used: (01) GTIN, (10) batch/lot, (17) expiry YYMMDD, (21) serial. A day of 00 means the last day of the month."},{"t":"Return and refund","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#returns","k":""},{"t":"Shift and cash-up","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#shift","k":"Expected cash = opening float + cash sales - cash refunds + cash in - cash out. A variance above the tenant threshold raises CashVarianceExceeded."},{"t":"Manager override (discounts, refunds, no-sale)","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#override","k":""},{"t":"Tax invoice and fiscal submission","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#tax-invoice","k":"Submitted documents are never changed. A correction is a credit or debit note."},{"t":"Price change reaching the registers","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#price-change","k":""},{"t":"Bulk product import","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#import","k":""},{"t":"Batch recall (pharmacy)","p":"Key flows","u":"flows.html#recall","k":"A manager blocks batch A123 of a SKU for every branch, with a reason. Inventory sets batch.status = BLOCKED and writes a batches change with high priority. Registers pull it on the next staff/settings/batches fast cycle "},{"t":"Glossary","p":"Glossary","u":"glossary.html","k":"One vocabulary for business people, developers and AI agents. Code, tables and UI use these words exactly."},{"t":"Business terms","p":"Glossary","u":"glossary.html#business","k":"Term Meaning Tenant One customer business (one subscription). It may own many branches. Branch One physical shop or outlet of a tenant, with its own stock location and registers. Register A logical till (counter) in a br"},{"t":"Tax and compliance","p":"Glossary","u":"glossary.html#tax-terms","k":"Term Meaning IRD Inland Revenue Department of Sri Lanka. VAT Value Added Tax. Rates are configured as tax rules, never hard-coded. Tax invoice An invoice in the format VAT law prescribes, issued by a VAT-registered busin"},{"t":"Technical terms","p":"Glossary","u":"glossary.html#tech-terms","k":"Term Meaning Modular monolith One deployable application divided into modules with enforced boundaries. Spring Modulith A library that verifies module boundaries and stores domain events reliably. SPI Service Provider In"},{"t":"Overview","p":"Overview","u":"index.html","k":"RetailOS is DevCity's point-of-sale and back-office platform for general retail, pharmacies and grocery stores. Registers keep selling when the internet drops, stock is tracked per batch and expiry date, and invoices fol"},{"t":"At a glance","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#at-a-glance","k":"Modular monolith One Spring Boot app with strict module boundaries. Split a module out only when measurements demand it. Offline-first Every register sells from its own SQLite database and syncs in the background. A sale"},{"t":"The big picture","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#big-picture","k":"Registers work locally and sync with one backend. Only the Tax module talks to the IRD."},{"t":"Reading paths","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#reading-paths","k":"Business analyst / product owner Requirements & scope → Roadmap → Screens & navigation → Industry extensions → Key flows Front-end / UI developer, designer Screens & navigation → UI design & wireframes → Technology stack"},{"t":"Key decisions","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#key-decisions","k":"Area Decision Why Record Shape Modular monolith (Spring Modulith) One developer and one database give real transactions across sales and stock. Boundaries are tested, so a module can be split out later. ADR-001 Register "},{"t":"Tech stack","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#tech-stack","k":"A summary of the main choices. The full list of every technology, with its version line, role, licence, cost and the rejected alternatives, is on Technology stack . Layer Choice Notes Backend Java 25 LTS, Spring Boot 4.x"},{"t":"Conventions used in these docs","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#conventions","k":""},{"t":"Release badges","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#badges","k":"MVP first sellable release R2 second release R3 third release Later backlog, not scheduled"},{"t":"Invariants (rules that must never break)","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#invariants","k":"Rules are numbered INV-nn and cited across all pages, in code comments and in tests. If code breaks an invariant, the code is wrong. The full list is in Guide for AI agents . The most important ones: ID Rule INV-01 Every"},{"t":"Assumptions and constraints","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#assumptions","k":"Market: Sri Lanka first. Prices are in LKR, the time zone is Asia/Colombo , and the UI is in English, Sinhala and Tamil. Team: one engineer at the start. Scope and technology are picked so one person can build, deploy an"},{"t":"Open questions","p":"Overview","u":"index.html#open-questions","k":"ID Question Affects Owner Q-01 When will the IRD publish the secured POS specification, and does it need certified hardware? Tax module, hardware bundles Product Q-02 What does the RAMIS e-invoicing API look like for pha"},{"t":"Backend modules","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html","k":"Each module owns its tables, exposes one public API interface and publishes events. If you need data from another module, call its API or listen to its events. Never query its tables ( INV-08 )."},{"t":"Module map","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html#map","k":"Module Package Owns Style Release Tenancy platform.tenancy tenant, branch, register, tenant_module, settings CRUD MVP Identity & access platform.iam app_user, role, permission, user_role, refresh_token, staff_pin CRUD + "},{"t":"Dependency rules","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html#dependencies","k":"Allowed direction: extensions → core → platform . Platform never depends on core, and core never depends on an extension. Core modules may call another core module's *Api interface only when they need an answer now (insi"},{"t":"Module details","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html#details","k":"Sales: records sales, returns and held bills Responsibility. Turns a register's completed sale into a permanent fact, allocates batches, and records returns linked to original lines. Owns the sale lifecycle. Public API S"},{"t":"Domain event catalog","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html#events","k":"Events are published through Spring Modulith's event publication registry, so they are stored in the same transaction as the change and retried until every listener succeeds ( ADR-007 ). Listeners must be idempotent. Eve"},{"t":"Error code catalog","p":"Backend modules","u":"modules.html#errors","k":"Every error returned by the API carries a stable code (see API errors ). Codes are searchable in logs. The prefix tells you which module to look in. Code HTTP Meaning AUTH-001 401 Token missing or expired AUTH-003 403 Pe"},{"t":"Offline & sync","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html","k":"Every sale follows the same path whether the network is up or down. The register sells from its own database, then a background engine pulls reference data and pushes facts. This is the largest technical risk in the prod"},{"t":"Who owns what","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#authority","k":"Data Authority Direction On disagreement Products, SKUs, barcodes, prices, tax rates Server Pull The server version overwrites the local copy Batches (open, this branch) and estimated stock Server Pull The local estimate"},{"t":"The path of one sale","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#sale-path","k":"The commit happens before printing. If the power fails after the commit, the sale exists and the receipt can be reprinted."},{"t":"Outbox item states","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#outbox-states","k":"BLOCKED items raise an alert in the support console. They are never dropped silently."},{"t":"Enrolling and bootstrapping a register","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#bootstrap","k":"A manager creates the register in the admin app and gets a one-time enrollment code , valid for 15 minutes. The register app generates a device key pair, held by Windows DPAPI or the Android Keystore, and calls POST /api"},{"t":"Pull: the change feed","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#pull","k":"GET /sync/v1/changes?scopes=catalog,prices,batches,staff,taxes,settings&cursor=184220&limit=1000 Authorization: Bearer <device+user token> X-Register-Id: 0190f3c2-... X-App-Version: 1.4.2 200 OK { \"cursor\": 185220, \"hasM"},{"t":"Push: sending facts","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#push","k":"POST /sync/v1/push { \"registerId\": \"0190f3c2-...\", \"items\": [ { \"kind\": \"CASH_SESSION_OPENED\", \"id\": \"0191a0...\", \"payload\": { ... } }, { \"kind\": \"SALE\", \"id\": \"0191a1...\", \"payload\": { \"receiptNo\": \"CMB01-R02-000154\", \""},{"t":"Receipt numbering","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#receipts","k":"Format: {branchCode}-{registerCode}-{seq:6} , e.g. CMB01-R02-000154 . Tax invoices use their own series, e.g. CMB01-R02-TI-000031 . The sequence is incremented inside the same local transaction that completes the sale, s"},{"t":"Offline guard rails","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#offline-rules","k":"Situation Register behaviour Offline for more than 24 h (configurable) A yellow banner says prices may be out of date. Selling continues. Offline for more than 72 h (configurable) A red banner. A manager PIN is needed ea"},{"t":"Clocks and dates","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#clock","k":"The register sends completedAt (device clock) and a monotonic deviceSeq . The server adds received_at . Every sync response includes the server time. If the device clock is off by more than 5 minutes, the register warns,"},{"t":"Failure scenarios","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#failures","k":"Failure What happens Recovery Power cut mid-sale SQLite in WAL mode: the sale is either fully committed or not there at all On restart the uncommitted cart is restored from cart_draft . A committed sale offers a receipt "},{"t":"Several registers in one branch","p":"Offline & sync","u":"offline-sync.html#multi-register","k":"Registers don't talk to each other. Each one sees other registers' sales through the server after both have synced, usually within a minute while online. During a long internet outage, stock estimates on each register dr"},{"t":"Monitoring & runbooks","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html","k":"You can't drive to every shop. RetailOS is built so that most problems can be seen, diagnosed and often fixed remotely: every register reports its health, every sale can be traced end to end, and every common failure has"},{"t":"Observability stack","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#observability","k":"Vendor-neutral: OpenTelemetry in the app means the backend can be swapped without code changes."},{"t":"Logging rules","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#logging","k":"Structured JSON to stdout with these fields: ts, level, msg, traceId, spanId, tenantId, branchId, registerId, userId, saleId, code . Log WARN or higher for every SaleException , BLOCKED outbox item, RLS error and auth fa"},{"t":"Key metrics and alerts","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#metrics","k":"Metric Why Alert when Severity sync_push_lag_seconds (per register: now − oldest pending sale) Unsynced sales are at risk > 6 h while the register's heartbeat is online High outbox_blocked_items A bug is stranding facts "},{"t":"Support console","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#support-console","k":"An internal page in the admin app, visible only to PLATFORM_SUPPORT with tenant consent. It shows: Per register: app version, last heartbeat, last successful pull and push, pending and blocked outbox counts, printer stat"},{"t":"Debugging: trace a sale end to end","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#debug-sale","k":"Every sale carries its UUID and a traceparent from the moment it's created on the register. Use either one to follow it. Start from the receipt. Receipt CMB01-R02-000154 → admin: Sales → search receipt . If it's found, y"},{"t":"Routine maintenance","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#maintenance","k":"Frequency Task Automated? Nightly Ledger check (rebuild balances, compare), audit chain check, expiry scan, catalog snapshot build, materialized view refresh, partition creation (3 months ahead) Yes (worker jobs) Daily R"},{"t":"Runbooks","p":"Monitoring & runbooks","u":"operations.html#runbooks","k":"RB-01 · A register isn't syncing Support console: last heartbeat. No heartbeat means a network or app problem in the shop. Ask the shop to open the register's status screen (it shows the connection test result). Heartbea"},{"t":"Requirements & scope","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html","k":"What RetailOS must do, for whom, and in which release. Features have IDs ( F-xxx ), business rules ( BR-xx ) and non-functional requirements ( NFR-xx ), so tickets, tests and code can cite them."},{"t":"Business goals","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#goals","k":"ID Goal Measure of success BG-1 Billing never stops in a shop Zero lost sales during internet or cloud outages. Checkout works offline for at least 72 hours. BG-2 Shops comply with Sri Lankan VAT invoicing Tax invoices a"},{"t":"Personas and roles","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#personas","k":"Persona Uses Cares about System role Shop owner Admin web, mobile dashboard Profit, theft, cash shortages, tax compliance OWNER Branch manager Admin web, register (overrides) Stock levels, staff, day-end cash-up, approvi"},{"t":"Scope by release","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#scope","k":"The MVP rule The MVP covers what a cashier needs every day and what a tax auditor will check. Back-office breadth comes later. With one engineer, every MVP item has to earn its place. MVP In scope Local-first Windows reg"},{"t":"Feature catalogue","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#features","k":"This catalogue follows the original DevCity feature list. Items marked red (\"later\") in the proposal keep that status unless the review moved them, which is noted in the last column."},{"t":"1. Sales and billing","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-sales","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-101 Scan barcode (1D and GS1 2D DataMatrix/QR) and search by name, SKU or generic name MVP Searches the local catalog, so it works offline. Requires 2D imager scanners. F-102 Cart: quantity, un"},{"t":"2. Inventory","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-inventory","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-201 Real-time stock deduction through the movement ledger MVP Deducted when the sale syncs. The register keeps its own local estimate. F-202 Low-stock alerts (per product per branch reorder lev"},{"t":"3. Customers (CRM)","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-crm","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-301 Customer profiles with purchase history MVP Personal data is minimised (PDPA, see Security ). F-302 Credit sales, credit limit, settlement, statement MVP BR-07. Common in Sri Lankan shops. "},{"t":"4. Reports and analytics","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-reports","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-401 Sales by day, week, month, product, category, cashier, branch MVP SQL and materialized views. F-402 Gross profit from snapshotted cost and price ( INV-10 ) MVP F-403 Stock on hand, valuatio"},{"t":"5. Employees","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-staff","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-501 Users, roles, fine-grained permissions, manager override by PIN MVP See the permission matrix . F-502 Shift open and close: opening float, cash in/out, counted cash, shortage or overage MVP"},{"t":"6. Cloud and multi-branch","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-cloud","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-601 Cloud backend, available anywhere MVP Was red in the proposal, but it is the architecture itself, so it is MVP. F-602 Offline billing with automatic sync MVP Moved from \"later\". See Offline"},{"t":"7. Hardware","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-hardware","k":"ID Device Release How it connects F-701 1D/2D barcode scanner MVP Acts as a USB/Bluetooth keyboard (HID). Must read GS1 DataMatrix. F-702 Thermal receipt printer, 80 mm and 58 mm MVP ESC/POS over USB, LAN (TCP 9100) or B"},{"t":"8. Integrations","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-integrations","k":"ID Integration Release Notes F-801 IRD RAMIS e-invoicing R3 Behind the Tax adapter. Built once the specification is published (Q-02). F-802 Secured POS (VAT Amendment Act No. 14 of 2026) R3 Fiscal adapter port designed i"},{"t":"9. Industry-specific features","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-industry","k":"These are delivered as extension modules. See Industry extensions for how they plug in. Industry Features Release General retail Core only: variants, barcodes, batches, promotions MVP Pharmacy Prescription capture, gener"},{"t":"10. Security and compliance","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-security","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-1001 Password + TOTP MFA (owners and admins), PIN for register staff MVP F-1002 Tamper-evident audit log (voids, refunds, overrides, price changes, drawer opens) MVP INV-09 F-1003 Card payments"},{"t":"11. Localisation and onboarding (new)","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#f-localisation","k":"ID Feature Release Notes F-1101 UI in English, Sinhala, Tamil; switchable per user MVP All text goes through i18n keys from the first screen. F-1102 Product names in three languages (optional fields) MVP F-1103 Tenant on"},{"t":"Key user stories","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#stories","k":"Acceptance criteria use Given/When/Then so they can become automated tests directly. US-01 · Sell while the internet is down (F-602, F-101) As a cashier, I want to keep billing when the internet is down, so customers are"},{"t":"Business rules","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#rules","k":"ID Rule BR-01 Each role has a maximum discount (percentage and amount). A larger discount needs a manager override, which is recorded with who, when and why. BR-02 Price snapshot: a line stores the unit price, discounts,"},{"t":"Non-functional requirements","p":"Requirements & scope","u":"requirements.html#nfr","k":"ID Quality Requirement NFR-01 Register speed Scan to line on screen in under 100 ms (p95) with 50,000 products in the local catalog. NFR-02 Checkout Complete to receipt printing starts in under 1.5 s (p95), online or off"},{"t":"Roadmap & phases","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html","k":"Build in vertical slices, put the local register in early, and put real shops on the product before launch. Each phase ends with a test that proves it works, not with a date. One engineer: be honest about time For one ex"},{"t":"MVP timeline","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#timeline","k":"Starting 1 Dec 2026, this lands general availability around Q4 2027, in time for the 2027/2028 market and the VAT secured-POS timeline."},{"t":"MVP phases and exit tests","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#phases","k":"Phase Builds Done when (exit test) P0 Setup ~2 weeks Monorepo, Gradle + pnpm workspaces, docker compose (Postgres, MinIO, Mailpit), CI pipeline, Spring Modulith skeleton with empty modules, React admin and register shell"},{"t":"Release 2 (about 4–6 months after launch)","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#r2","k":"Android register (Capacitor shell + device plugins) Pharmacy module Grocery module (PLU, scale, labels) Promotions engine Purchase orders Stock transfers Supplier returns Exchanges as one flow Loyalty points E-mail recei"},{"t":"Release 3 (timed to IRD publications)","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#r3","k":"RAMIS e-invoicing adapter Secured POS adapter (spec dependent) Semi-integrated card terminals LankaQR dynamic QR QuickBooks / Xero / Zoho connectors SMS + WhatsApp receipts and offers Gift cards and store credit Membersh"},{"t":"Later (not scheduled)","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#later","k":"AI forecasting and reorder suggestions E-commerce stock sync Delivery-app orders Self-checkout kiosk Restaurant module Salon module Fingerprint login Local-network register-to-register sync Data for AI features is alread"},{"t":"Team plan","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#team","k":"When Role Why Now 1 full-stack engineer (architect + developer) Builds P0–P3. Uses this documentation and AGENTS.md to get the most out of AI coding assistants. From P4 +1 engineer (front-end / register focus) Checkout a"},{"t":"Delivery risks","p":"Roadmap & phases","u":"roadmap.html#risks","k":"Risk Impact Mitigation Single engineer (bus factor 1) All knowledge in one head. Illness or departure stops the project. This documentation, ADRs, AGENTS.md, tests as specification, a second hire by P4 Sync bugs duplicat"},{"t":"Security architecture","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html","k":"A POS handles money, stock, staff and customer data for many businesses at once. The two worst outcomes are one shop seeing another shop's data, and undetected manipulation of sales or cash. Every control below exists to"},{"t":"Threat model (STRIDE)","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#threats","k":"TB = trust boundary. The shop device is treated as hostile: it can be stolen, shared or tampered with. Threat Example Controls S poofing A cashier uses a manager's identity. A fake register pushes sales. Personal PINs wi"},{"t":"Authentication","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#authn","k":"Actor Method Details Owner, admin, accountant (web) E-mail + password + TOTP MFA MFA required for OWNER and ADMIN , optional for others. Passwords: at least 10 characters, checked against a breached-password list (NIST 8"},{"t":"Tokens and sessions","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#tokens","k":"Access token: signed JWT (EdDSA or ES256), 10-minute lifetime. Claims: sub, tid (tenant), bid (branch), did (device), roles, ver . Kept in memory, never in localStorage . Refresh token: opaque, stored hashed on the serve"},{"t":"Authorisation and permission matrix","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#rbac","k":"Roles are bundles of fine-grained permissions. Tenants can create custom roles from the same permissions. Checks run on the server for every request, and on the register for offline actions. Permission Owner Manager Cash"},{"t":"Tenant isolation","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#tenant-isolation","k":"Token: the tenant comes only from the signed token, never from a URL or body. Application: a request filter sets TenantContext , and repositories always filter by tenant_id . Database: set_config('app.tenant_id', …, true"},{"t":"Register and device security","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#register-security","k":"Control Windows (Electron) Android (Capacitor) Local DB encryption SQLCipher (AES-256). Key wrapped with DPAPI (machine + user scope). SQLCipher via the community plugin. Key in the Android Keystore. App integrity Code-s"},{"t":"Encryption and secrets","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#data-protection","k":"In transit: TLS 1.2/1.3 everywhere, HSTS on the admin domain, TLS between the app and the database when they're on different hosts. At rest: encrypted disks and volumes on the database and object storage (provider-manage"},{"t":"Audit logging","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#audit","k":"The audit log answers \"who did what, when, from which device, and who approved it\". It is tamper-evident: audit_log(seq, tenant_id, occurred_at, actor_id, approver_id, device_id, action, entity, entity_id, before jsonb, "},{"t":"Payments and PCI-DSS","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#pci","k":"Stay out of PCI scope ( INV-11 ) Card numbers, CVV and track data never enter RetailOS: no screen, API, log or database ever sees them. In the MVP the card terminal runs standalone, and the cashier records the approval c"},{"t":"Application security controls","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#appsec","k":"Area Control Input validation Bean Validation on every DTO. Explicit allowlists for sort fields. Parameterised SQL only, never string-built. Output React escapes by default. dangerouslySetInnerHTML is banned by a lint ru"},{"t":"Secure development lifecycle","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#sdlc","k":"Stage Tool (free or low cost) Gate Secrets gitleaks (pre-commit and CI) Any finding blocks the merge SAST Semgrep or CodeQL High findings block the merge Dependencies Renovate/Dependabot + OSV-Scanner Critical CVEs block"},{"t":"Privacy and data protection","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#privacy","k":"Sri Lanka's Personal Data Protection Act, No. 9 of 2022, applies to customer and staff data. RetailOS is the processor , and each shop is the controller for its customers. Confirm current obligations with legal counsel, "},{"t":"Incident response","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#incident","k":"Detect: alerts for auth failure spikes, RLS errors, audit chain breaks, unusual exports, register tokens used from new countries. Contain: revoke tokens (bump user or tenant ver ), lock devices, rotate secrets, disable a"},{"t":"Security checklist for every pull request","p":"Security architecture","u":"security.html#security-checklist","k":"New endpoint has @PreAuthorize with a specific permission, plus a test proving a cashier token is refused. New table has tenant_id , an RLS policy and a row in TenantIsolationIT . No secrets, tokens, PINs or personal dat"},{"t":"Stitch prompts","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html","k":"Copy-ready prompts for designing every RetailOS screen in Google Stitch. Paste the master prompt first so Stitch learns the product and design system. Then add screens one at a time, and ask for a dark version of each. M"},{"t":"Brand palette and usage rules","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#palette","k":"#3772FF Primary · brand, buttons, selection, info #22C55E Success · totals, synced, complete #272932 Charcoal · text, dark surfaces #FDFFFC Off-white · light background #FF7F11 Warning · offline, expiry, low stock #FF1B1"},{"t":"Contrast-safe usage (measured)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#contrast","k":"Pairing Contrast Rule White text on #3772FF 4.2 : 1 OK for button labels at 16 px semibold or larger (and all register buttons, which are 18 px+). For small blue link text on light backgrounds use #2A5BD9 (5.8 : 1). Whit"},{"t":"Full token set","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#tokens","k":"Token Light Dark Background #FDFFFC #1E2028 Surface (cards, panels) #FFFFFF #272932 Surface subtle / raised #F3F5F9 #31343F Border #E4E7EC #3A3D4A Text / muted text #272932 / #6B7080 #FDFFFC / #A3A8B8 Primary (fill) / pr"},{"t":"How to use these prompts in Stitch","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#workflow","k":"One Stitch project per app: \"RetailOS Register\" (Web mode), \"RetailOS Admin\" (Web mode), \"RetailOS Mobile\" (Mobile mode), \"RetailOS Console\" (Web mode). This keeps each project's context focused. First message in each pr"},{"t":"Master prompt (paste first in every project)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#master","k":"Design \"RetailOS by DevCity\", a modern point-of-sale (POS) and back-office system for retail shops, pharmacies and grocery stores in Sri Lanka. It must feel fast, calm and trustworthy, in a clean modern SaaS style simila"},{"t":"Short master prompt","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#master-short","k":"RetailOS by DevCity: modern POS + back office for Sri Lankan retail, pharmacy and grocery. Clean SaaS style (Shopify POS / Linear). Light theme: bg #FDFFFC, cards #FFFFFF, border #E4E7EC, text #272932, muted #6B7080. Pri"},{"t":"Dark variant prompt (after each screen)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#dark","k":"Create a dark mode version of this exact screen with the same layout and content. Dark tokens: background #1E2028, cards/panels #272932, raised elements #31343F, borders #3A3D4A, text #FDFFFC, muted text #A3A8B8. Primary"},{"t":"Register app prompts","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#register","k":"Stitch project: RetailOS Register , Web mode. Every prompt starts with the frame size. For the Android tablet (R2), re-run the same prompts with \"1280×800 Android tablet landscape, bottom sheets instead of modals\"."},{"t":"R-01 · Device setup","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r01","k":"Screen R-01 \"Device setup\" for the RetailOS register, full-screen desktop app 1366x768, no browser chrome. A centered 4-step wizard card with a progress stepper: 1 Enter enrollment code, 2 Download catalog, 3 Test hardwa"},{"t":"R-02 · PIN sign-in","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r02","k":"Screen R-02 \"Sign in\" for the RetailOS register, 1366x768 full-screen. Top bar: RetailOS logo (blue #3772FF mark), \"City Pharmacy & Mart · Colombo 03 · Register R02\", on the right a green badge \"Online · synced 10:41\" an"},{"t":"R-03 · Open shift","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r03","k":"Screen R-03 \"Open shift\" for the RetailOS register, 1366x768. Title \"Open your shift, Sachini\". Left: a denomination counter table with rows Rs 5000, 1000, 500, 100, 50, 20, coins (each with minus/plus steppers and a qua"},{"t":"R-04 · Checkout (most important)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r04","k":"Screen R-04 \"Checkout\", the main sale screen of the RetailOS register, 1366x768, no page scroll. TOP BAR (48px): menu icon, \"CMB01 · R02\", cashier chip \"Sachini K. · shift 3h 12m\", spacer, orange warning badge \"Offline ·"},{"t":"R-05 · Product lookup","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r05","k":"Screen R-05 \"Product lookup\" as a large modal over the checkout screen (dimmed background), 1366x768. Search field with text \"paracet\" and filter chips: All, Name, Generic, SKU. Results table: product name (with a Sinhal"},{"t":"R-06 · Batch picker","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r06","k":"Screen R-06 \"Choose batch\" as a medium modal over checkout. Title \"Choose batch · Paracetamol 500mg (10s)\". Three selectable rows as cards: B1 \"exp 03/2027 · 48 in stock · Rs 30.00\" with a green badge \"FEFO, sells first\""},{"t":"R-07 · Line editor + R-08 manager override","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r07","k":"Screen R-07 \"Edit line\" as a right-side drawer over checkout for \"Milk powder 400g\". Fields: quantity stepper with unit select (piece/box), unit price (read-only, lock icon), line discount with a % / Rs toggle and quick "},{"t":"R-09 · Customer","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r09","k":"Screen R-09 \"Select customer\" modal over checkout. Search by name or phone with recent customers listed: name, masked phone 077****321, tags (Credit, Loyalty). Selected customer detail card: Perera Stores, credit limit R"},{"t":"R-10 · Payment","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r10","k":"Screen R-10 \"Payment\" for the RetailOS register, 1366x768. Top: \"← Back to cart (Esc)\" and receipt number \"CMB01-R02-000155\". Left half: \"Amount due\" card with \"Rs 2,349.00\" very large; four large payment type buttons wi"},{"t":"R-11 · Sale complete","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r11","k":"Screen R-11 \"Sale complete\", full screen, celebratory but calm. Center: a large green #22C55E circle with a charcoal check icon, \"Sale complete\", receipt \"CMB01-R02-000155\", a big \"Change due Rs 651.00\" (green text #1580"},{"t":"R-12 · Held bills","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r12","k":"Screen R-12 \"Held bills\" modal: a list of parked sales as cards with time held, cashier, item count, total, optional note (\"Customer went to ATM\"), and buttons Resume (primary) and Discard (red text). Empty state illustr"},{"t":"R-13 · Returns","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r13","k":"Screen R-13 \"Return items\", 1366x768. Step 1 already done: scanned receipt \"CMB01-R02-000154 · 18 Nov 2026 · Rs 3,120.00\". Main table of the original lines with columns Product, Sold, Already returned, Return qty (steppe"},{"t":"R-14 · Sales history","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r14","k":"Screen R-14 \"Today's sales\" for the register: filter chips (This register, Whole branch), search by receipt number, and a table: time, receipt number, cashier, items, payment type icons, total, sync status badge (green \""},{"t":"R-15 · Cash in / out","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r15","k":"Screen R-15 \"Cash in / out\" modal: segmented control Cash in | Cash out | Safe drop; amount input with keypad; reason select (Petty cash: transport, Float top-up, Safe drop, Supplier COD); note; current drawer estimate s"},{"t":"R-16 · Close shift","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r16","k":"Screen R-16 \"Close shift\" for the register, 1366x768, a 3-step stepper: 1 Count cash (active), 2 Review, 3 Print Z-report. Left: denomination counter (Rs 5000 x 3, 1000 x 14, 500 x 9, 100 x 22, coins 340.00). Right: \"Cou"},{"t":"R-17 · Goods receiving","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r17","k":"Screen R-17 \"Receive goods\" on the register, 1366x768. Header fields: supplier select \"Hemas Pharmaceuticals\", supplier invoice no, date. Large scan field \"Scan 2D code (GS1) or barcode\". A highlighted toast: \"Scanned: G"},{"t":"R-18 · Price & stock check","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r18","k":"Screen R-18 \"Price check\": a single big scan field, then a large product card showing name in English and Sinhala, price \"Rs 320.00\" very large, unit price per kg, stock estimate badge, batches with expiry, and active pr"},{"t":"R-19 · Status & diagnostics","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r19","k":"Screen R-19 \"Status & diagnostics\" for the register: a grid of status cards each with icon, value and badge: Connection (orange \"Offline since 09:12\"), Last sync push/pull times, Waiting to sync 12 (orange), Blocked item"},{"t":"R-20 · Device settings","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r20","k":"Screen R-20 \"Register settings\" with left vertical tabs: Printer, Receipt, Scanner, Quick keys, Language, Training mode. Show the Printer tab: printer type (USB / Network / Bluetooth), IP 192.168.1.50 port 9100, paper wi"},{"t":"R-21 · Customer display","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r21","k":"Screen R-21 \"Customer display\", a second screen 1024x600 facing the customer: shop logo and name, the last scanned item large (\"Basmati rice 1.250 kg · Rs 800.00\"), a running list of items, a very large total \"Rs 2,349.0"},{"t":"R-30, R-31 · Pharmacy panels (R2)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r30","k":"Screen R-30 \"Prescription details\", a modal opened before completing a sale that contains prescription items. Fields: prescriber name, prescriber registration no., prescription date, Rx number, patient (linked customer),"},{"t":"R-32, R-33 · Grocery panels (R2)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-r32","k":"Screen R-32 \"Weigh item\" panel on checkout: PLU code entry keypad, a large live scale reading \"1.250 kg\" with a \"stable\" green badge, tare button, item found \"Carrots · Rs 320.00/kg\", and the calculated price \"Rs 400.00\""},{"t":"Admin web prompts","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#admin","k":"Stitch project: RetailOS Admin , Web mode, 1440×900. Every admin screen uses the same app shell, so describe the shell once (prompt A-shell), then refer to it."},{"t":"A-shell · Admin app shell","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-ashell","k":"Create the RetailOS Admin app shell at 1440x900 that every later admin screen will use. Left sidebar (240px, white, border right #E4E7EC): RetailOS logo, branch switcher \"All branches ▾\", navigation with Lucide icons: Da"},{"t":"A-01 to A-03 · Login, MFA, reset","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a01","k":"Screen A-01 \"Sign in\" for RetailOS Admin, 1440x900, split layout: left 45% a brand panel in #3772FF with the RetailOS logo, tagline \"Sell anywhere, even offline\" and a soft illustration of a shop counter; right a sign-in"},{"t":"A-05 · Onboarding wizard","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a05","k":"Screen A-05 \"Set up your business\", a full-page onboarding wizard with a left vertical stepper: Business details, VAT & tax, Branches, Registers, Receipt, Import products, Invite staff. Show \"Branches\" active: list of br"},{"t":"A-10 · Dashboard","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a10","k":"Screen A-10 \"Dashboard\" inside the RetailOS Admin shell. Row 1: four KPI cards: Sales today \"Rs 486,200\" with a green \"+8% vs last Tuesday\" trend chip, Transactions 612, Average basket Rs 794, Gross margin 18.4%. Row 2: "},{"t":"A-10m · Owner mobile dashboard (Mobile project)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a10m","k":"Mobile screen (Stitch Mobile mode) \"Today\" for shop owners in the RetailOS Admin mobile web. Top: greeting \"Good morning, Malini\", branch switcher chip. A horizontally scrollable KPI carousel (Sales today Rs 486,200 with"},{"t":"A-20 · Products list","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a20","k":"Screen A-20 \"Products\" in the RetailOS Admin shell. Page actions: \"Import\" (secondary), \"Export\", primary \"Add product\". Filter bar: search, Category, Brand, Tax class, Status, \"Low stock only\" toggle. Data table with a "},{"t":"A-21 · Product editor","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a21","k":"Screen A-21 \"Product: Paracetamol 500mg\" in the RetailOS Admin shell with breadcrumb Catalog › Products. Tabs: General, Variants & SKUs, Barcodes & units, Prices, Stock & batches, Pharmacy, History. Show the General tab:"},{"t":"A-22, A-24 · Categories, brands, units","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a22","k":"Screen A-22 \"Categories & brands\": two-column layout. Left: a draggable category tree (Pharmacy › Pain relief, Antibiotics; Grocery › Rice, Dairy; Household) with item counts and a colour dot used for register quick keys"},{"t":"A-23 · Import wizard","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a23","k":"Screen A-23 \"Import products\" wizard in the RetailOS Admin shell, horizontal stepper: Template, Upload, Map columns, Preview, Import. Show the Preview step: summary cards \"1,240 new\" (green), \"312 updated\" (blue), \"18 er"},{"t":"A-30 to A-33 · Pricing","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a30","k":"Screen A-30 \"Price lists\": tabs Retail, Wholesale; table of SKUs with current price, scheduled new price with \"from 20 Nov 00:00\" chip, branch overrides indicator; primary \"Schedule price change\". Then screen A-31 \"Bulk "},{"t":"A-40, A-41 · Stock and batches","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a40","k":"Screen A-40 \"Stock on hand\" in the RetailOS Admin shell: branch selector, search, filters (category, negative stock, near expiry). Table grouped by product with expandable batch rows: batch no, expiry (orange badge if un"},{"t":"A-42 · Goods receipt","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a42","k":"Screen A-42 \"Goods receipt GRN-2291\" in the RetailOS Admin shell: status chip \"Draft\", supplier and invoice fields, a scan field for GS1 2D codes, and an editable lines grid (product, batch, expiry, quantity, unit, unit "},{"t":"A-43, A-44, A-45 · Adjustments, counts, expiry","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a43","k":"Screen A-43 \"New stock adjustment\": product/batch picker, quantity +/-, reason code (Damaged, Theft, Expired write-off, Found), note, approval notice above Rs 5,000. Then screen A-44 \"Stock count · Pain relief shelf\": co"},{"t":"A-46 to A-48 · Transfers, purchase orders, suppliers","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a46","k":"Screen A-46 \"Stock transfer TR-0045\": from CMB01 to KDY01, status stepper Requested → Shipped → Received, lines with requested/shipped/received quantities. Then screen A-47 \"Purchase order PO-0112\": supplier, expected da"},{"t":"A-50, A-51 · Sales history and sale detail","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a50","k":"Screen A-50 \"Sales\" in the RetailOS Admin shell: date range picker, filters (branch, register, cashier, payment type, customer), search by receipt number, table with time, receipt, branch/register, cashier, items, paymen"},{"t":"A-53 · Sale exceptions queue","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a53","k":"Screen A-53 \"Sale exceptions\" in the RetailOS Admin shell: filter chips by type (Negative stock, Price mismatch, Expired batch sold, Clock difference, Receipt collision), branch, age. A list on the left with type badges "},{"t":"A-55 · Shifts & cash","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a55","k":"Screen A-55 \"Shifts & cash\": table of shifts (register, cashier, opened, closed, expected, counted, difference). Differences colored: green 0, orange small, red large. Selected shift drawer with a Z-report summary, cash "},{"t":"A-60 to A-62 · Customers, credit, loyalty","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a60","k":"Screen A-60 \"Customers\": table with name, phone (masked), tags, credit outstanding, last visit, and \"Merge duplicates\" action. Then screen A-61 \"Customer: Perera Stores\": profile card, credit summary (limit Rs 100,000, o"},{"t":"A-65 to A-67 · Tax","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a65","k":"Screen A-65 \"Tax documents\": tabs Tax invoices, Credit notes, Debit notes; table with number, date, buyer and buyer VAT number, value, VAT, total, e-invoice status chip (Not applicable / Pending / Sent / Failed) and PDF "},{"t":"A-70 · Report centre","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a70","k":"Screen A-70 \"Reports\": a left list of report categories (Sales, Stock, Cash, Customers, Tax, Pharmacy) and a report gallery of cards (Daily sales, Sales by product, Margin, Stock valuation, Expiry, Z-reports, Credit agei"},{"t":"A-80 to A-84 · Settings","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a80","k":"Screen A-80 \"Settings · Business\": settings layout with a left settings nav (Business, Branches & registers, Users & roles, Devices, Receipts, Modules, Integrations, Audit log, Data & privacy, Subscription). Business for"},{"t":"A-82 · Users & roles","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a82","k":"Screen A-82 \"Users & roles\" with tabs Users and Roles. Users: table with avatar, name, email, roles per branch chips, MFA status, last active, \"Invite user\" primary button. Roles tab: role list on the left (Owner, Manage"},{"t":"A-85 to A-90 · Modules, integrations, audit, privacy, subscription, profile","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a85","k":"Screen A-85 \"Modules\": cards for Pharmacy, Grocery (and greyed \"Restaurant · coming later\", \"Salon · coming later\") with icon, description, features list, status switch and \"Configure\". Then screen A-86 \"Integrations\": c"},{"t":"A-100 to A-103 · Pharmacy and grocery admin (R2)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#p-a100","k":"Screen A-100 \"Prescriptions\": table with Rx number, date, patient, prescriber, items, pharmacist, linked sale, a thumbnail of the prescription photo, and a detail drawer. Then screen A-101 \"Controlled drug register\": dru"},{"t":"Platform console prompts (DevCity internal)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#console","k":"Project \"RetailOS Console\", Web mode 1440x900, same design system but with a charcoal #272932 sidebar to distinguish internal tools, and a \"DevCity internal\" badge. Screen P-01 \"Tenants\": table with tenant name, plan, mo"},{"t":"State and edge-case prompts","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#states","k":"For the current screen, create 4 additional variants side by side with the same layout: 1) Loading: skeleton placeholders, no spinners over content. 2) Empty: friendly empty state with a one-line explanation and the next"},{"t":"Refinement prompts (one change at a time)","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#refine","k":"Increase all touch targets on this screen to at least 48px and the keypad keys to 64px, without changing the layout. Reduce visual noise: use only one primary blue button, make other actions secondary or ghost, and remov"},{"t":"From Stitch to code","p":"Stitch prompts","u":"stitch-prompts.html#handoff","k":"Export each accepted screen to Figma and name frames with the screen ID (\"R-04 Checkout · light\", \"R-04 Checkout · dark\"). Put the tokens above into packages/ui/tokens (CSS variables + Tailwind theme). Generated Stitch c"},{"t":"Technology stack","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html","k":"This page lists every technology used to build, test, ship and run RetailOS: what each one does in the system, why it was chosen, and what was rejected. If a library is not on this page, add it here (with a reason) in th"},{"t":"Stack at a glance","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#overview","k":"Two languages in total: Java on the server, TypeScript everywhere else. Kotlin appears only in a thin Android device plugin."},{"t":"Languages","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#languages","k":"Language Version line Used for Why Java 25 LTS Backend Long-term support until at least 2030. Virtual threads, records and pattern matching. A strong ecosystem for transactional business systems. TypeScript 5.x Admin web"},{"t":"Backend","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#backend","k":"Technology Version line Role in RetailOS Why chosen Licence Spring Boot 4.0.x Application framework, configuration, Actuator health and metrics Mature and well documented, and AI assistants know it well. The 3.x line is "},{"t":"Database and storage","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#database","k":"Technology Version line Role Notes PostgreSQL 18 System of record for all tenants Native uuidv7() , row-level security, declarative partitioning, materialized views. Free, and every cloud offers it managed. pg_trgm exten"},{"t":"Front-end (shared by admin and register)","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#frontend","k":"Technology Version line Role Why chosen React 19.x UI library for admin and register Largest ecosystem and hiring pool. The same skills cover both apps. Vite 7.x Dev server and bundler Fast, simple, and works inside Elec"},{"t":"Register app and shells","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#register","k":"Technology Platform Role Notes Electron (current stable line) Windows Desktop shell for the React register Hardened: context isolation, sandbox, typed IPC allowlist ( Security ). Upgrade every few months to stay on a sup"},{"t":"Testing and quality tools","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#testing","k":"Tool Used for JUnit Jupiter + AssertJ + Mockito Backend unit tests Testcontainers (PostgreSQL 18) Integration tests against a real database: RLS, allocation concurrency, migrations Spring Modulith test support Module tes"},{"t":"DevOps, build and hosting","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#devops","k":"Technology Role Cost Git + GitHub (private repo) Source control, pull requests, issues Free tier is enough at the start GitHub Actions CI/CD (the scripts live in infra/ci/ , so they're portable to GitLab CI and others) F"},{"t":"Security tooling","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#security-tools","k":"Tool Stage Purpose gitleaks Pre-commit + CI Blocks committed secrets Semgrep (or GitHub CodeQL) CI Static code analysis for Java and TypeScript OSV-Scanner + Renovate CI + weekly Vulnerable dependency detection, automati"},{"t":"Observability","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#observability","k":"Technology Role Cost-efficient option OpenTelemetry (Java agent or Spring Boot starter, collector) Traces, metrics and logs in a vendor-neutral format Free. Lets you switch backends without code changes. Micrometer Appli"},{"t":"External services","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#external","k":"Service Used for Release Selection rule Transactional e-mail provider Password reset, MFA setup, e-mail receipts, reports MVP SMTP or API with good delivery and a free tier. Hidden behind a MailSender port. Sri Lankan SM"},{"t":"Developer tools","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#dev-tools","k":"IntelliJ IDEA (backend) VS Code (front-end) Docker Desktop JDK 25 (Eclipse Temurin) Node.js 22 LTS pnpm DBeaver / pgAdmin DB Browser for SQLite Bruno (API collections in git) Claude Code / AI coding assistant with AGENTS"},{"t":"Reference hardware","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#hardware","k":"Device Minimum spec / requirement Windows register PC Windows 10/11 x64, 4 GB RAM, SSD, 1366×768 or larger (touch optional) Android register tablet R2 Android 10+, 3 GB RAM, 10\" screen, USB-OTG or Bluetooth Receipt print"},{"t":"Considered and rejected","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#rejected","k":"Option Instead of Why not (for now) Microservices, Kubernetes Modular monolith, Docker Too much operations work for one engineer ( ADR-001 , ADR-009 ) Kafka / RabbitMQ Spring Modulith event registry Nothing needs a broke"},{"t":"Skills needed to build it","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#skills","k":"Area Must know Nice to have Backend Java 21+, Spring Boot, JPA, SQL and PostgreSQL transactions/locking, REST, Spring Security basics Spring Modulith, Testcontainers, performance tuning Front-end TypeScript, React, state"},{"t":"Version and upgrade policy","p":"Technology stack","u":"tech-stack.html#upgrades","k":"Runtimes: Java and Node stay on LTS lines. Move to the next LTS within 6 months of its release. Frameworks: stay within the supported window of Spring Boot, Electron and React. Electron needs upgrading every few months t"},{"t":"UI design & wireframes","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html","k":"How RetailOS should look and behave: the design rules, the shared component library, keyboard and touch conventions, and low-fidelity wireframes of the screens that matter most. The full screen list is on Screens & navig"},{"t":"Design principles","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#principles","k":"# Principle In practice U1 Speed at the counter beats beauty The scan field is always focused. The most common action is one key. No confirmation dialogs for routine actions. Undo instead of \"Are you sure?\". U2 Readable "},{"t":"Layouts and screen sizes","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#layouts","k":"Target Sizes Layout rules Windows register 1366×768 (design size), at least 1024×768, up to 1920×1080. Touch optional. Two panes: cart about 60% on the left, actions and totals about 40% on the right. Top status bar of 4"},{"t":"Typography and languages","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#typography","k":"Fonts: Noto Sans for Latin, plus Noto Sans Sinhala and Noto Sans Tamil, bundled with the apps (no CDN, works offline). Tabular numerals for prices and quantities so columns line up. Scale (register): 14 small · 16 body ·"},{"t":"Colour and status semantics","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#colour","k":"Brand palette RetailOS uses primary #3772FF , success #22C55E , charcoal #272932 , off-white #FDFFFC , warning #FF7F11 and error #FF1B1C . The exact light and dark tokens and the contrast-safe text shades are on Google S"},{"t":"Component library (packages/ui)","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#components","k":"Group Components Notes Basics Button, IconButton, Link, Badge, Tag, Tooltip, Avatar, Icon (Lucide), Spinner, Skeleton Button sizes sm/md/lg/xl (xl = keypad, Pay) Inputs TextField, NumberField, MoneyField, QuantityField, "},{"t":"Register keyboard map","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#shortcuts","k":"Key Action Key Action F1 Help / shortcut sheet F7 Recall held bill F2 Product search F8 Return F3 Customer F9 Cash in / out F4 Change quantity / weight F10 Pay F5 Discount (line, or bill with Shift ) F12 Manager function"},{"t":"Screen states","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#states","k":"Every screen and data component must design all of these, not only the \"happy\" state: State Register Admin Loading Rare (local data). Skeleton for slow lookups over 200 ms. Skeleton rows/tiles. Never a blank page. Empty "},{"t":"Accessibility","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#accessibility","k":"WCAG 2.2 AA target for the admin web. The register meets contrast, focus and target-size rules. A visible focus ring on everything, and a logical tab order. Modals trap focus and return it on close. Radix primitives give"},{"t":"Wireframes","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wireframes","k":""},{"t":"R-02 · Sign-in","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-signin","k":"RetailOS · CMB01 · Register R02 Online · synced 10:41 සිං | தமி | EN Who's working? NP Nimal P. SK Sachini K. RF Rizwan F. MJ Manager Enter PIN · Sachini K. ● ● ● ○ 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 ⌫ 0 OK Device WIN-CMB01-02 · v1.6.0 ·"},{"t":"R-04 · Checkout","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-checkout","k":"☰ CMB01 · R02 Sachini K. · shift 3h 12m Offline · 12 sales waiting Printer ready 🔍 Scan barcode or search name / generic / SKU … (F2) Cart · 4 lines 1. Panadol 500mg (10s) B2 · exp 09/27 2 × 32.00 = 64.00 2. Amoxicillin "},{"t":"R-06 · Batch picker","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-batch","k":"Choose batch · Panadol 500mg (10s) Esc B1 · exp 03/2027 · 48 in stock FEFO Rs 30.00 B2 · exp 09/2027 · 120 in stock Rs 32.00 B0 · exp 10/2026 · expired Blocked Shown only when open batches have different prices. Tip: sca"},{"t":"R-10 · Payment","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-payment","k":"← Back to cart (Esc) Receipt CMB01-R02-000155 Amount due Rs 2,349.00 Cash F1 Card F2 LankaQR F3 Credit F4 Payments Card · approval 482913 1,000.00 Cash 2,000.00 Change Rs 651.00 Tax invoice ☐ Customer needs a VAT tax inv"},{"t":"R-16 · Close shift (blind count)","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-close-shift","k":"Close shift · Sachini K. · opened 07:58 Step 1 of 3: count cash Notes and coins Rs 5000 × 3 Rs 1000 × 14 Rs 500 × 9 Rs 100 × 22 Coins total 340.00 Counted cash Rs 36,040.00 Expected amount and variance are shown after yo"},{"t":"A-10 · Admin dashboard","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-dashboard","k":"RetailOS Admin All branches ▾ 🔍 Search · 🔔 3 · Owner ▾ Dashboard Catalog Pricing Inventory Purchasing Sales Customers Tax Reports Settings Sales today Rs 486,200 +8% vs last Tue Transactions 612 Avg basket Rs 794 Gross m"},{"t":"A-21 · Product editor","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-product","k":"Catalog › Products › Panadol 500mg Cancel Save General · Variants & SKUs · Barcodes & units · Prices · Stock & batches · Pharmacy · History Names English Panadol 500mg සිංහල පැනඩෝල් 500mg தமிழ் பனடோல் 500mg Category / Br"},{"t":"A-53 · Sale exceptions queue","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-exceptions","k":"Sales › Exceptions Type: all ▾ Branch: all ▾ Open ▾ 7 open NEGATIVE_STOCK CMB01-R02-000154 · Anchor 400g 2 h ago PRICE_MISMATCH KDY01-R01-003310 · Sugar 1kg 5 h ago EXPIRED_BATCH_SOLD GAL01-R01-000981 1 d ago CLOCK_SKEW "},{"t":"D-01 · Sales receipt (80 mm)","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#wf-receipt","k":"CITY PHARMACY & MART No. 12, Galle Road, Colombo 3 VAT Reg: 123456789-7000 ☎ 011 2xx xxxx ------------------------------------------ Receipt : CMB01-R02-000155 Date : 19/11/2026 10:46 Cashier: Sachini -------------------"},{"t":"UI checklist for every screen","p":"UI design & wireframes","u":"ui-design.html#ui-checklist","k":"Screen ID in the file header and the page title (for support and search). All strings are i18n keys. Checked in si and ta at the smallest supported size. Loading, empty, error, offline and permission states designed and "},{"t":"Screens & navigation","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html","k":"RetailOS has three front-ends plus printed documents. This page lists every screen with an ID, who uses it, which release it ships in and how it behaves offline. It also specifies the screens that matter most in detail. "},{"t":"The front-ends","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#apps","k":"Register app R-xx The counter. Cashiers, pharmacists and managers. Windows (MVP) and Android (R2). Fully offline. Optimised for speed, scanning and touch plus keyboard. ~21 screens Admin web A-xx The back office. Owners,"},{"t":"Register app","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#register","k":""},{"t":"Register navigation","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#register-flow","k":"Checkout is the home screen. Everything else is one key or one tap away and returns to checkout."},{"t":"Register screen inventory","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#register-inventory","k":"ID Screen Purpose Who Release Offline R-01 Device setup Enter enrollment code, download catalog, test printer, drawer and scanner Manager / installer MVP Needs internet once R-02 Sign-in (PIN) Pick user tile, enter PIN, "},{"t":"Key register screens in detail","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#register-specs","k":"R-04 Checkout (home screen) Goal Ring up a typical basket of 5 items in under 20 seconds with a scanner, with no mouse needed. Layout Top bar: branch/register, cashier, shift time, sync status, menu. Left (≈60%): scan/se"},{"t":"Admin web","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#admin","k":""},{"t":"Admin sitemap","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#admin-sitemap","k":"Left sidebar navigation with these 10 sections. Menu items the user has no permission for are hidden, and the server checks again ( RBAC )."},{"t":"Admin screen inventory","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#admin-inventory","k":"ID Screen Purpose / key elements Main roles Release Access A-01 Login E-mail, password, language, \"forgot password\" All MVP A-02 MFA setup / verify QR code for an authenticator app, recovery codes, 6-digit verify Owner, "},{"t":"Key admin screens in detail","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#admin-specs","k":"A-10 Dashboard Top row (KPI tiles) Sales today · transactions · average basket · gross margin % · compared with the same day last week Middle Hourly sales chart (today vs last week). Sales by branch (when there is more t"},{"t":"Platform console (DevCity internal)","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#console","k":"ID Screen Purpose Release P-01 Tenants List, plan, modules, status, created, branch and register counts MVP P-02 Tenant detail Health summary, open exceptions, import errors, fiscal status, support-access request MVP P-0"},{"t":"Printed and generated documents","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#documents","k":"ID Document Format Contents Release D-01 Sales receipt 80/58 mm thermal Logo, business, branch, receipt number + barcode, date/time, cashier, lines, discounts, tax summary, payments, change, footer, return policy. en/si/"},{"t":"Which roles see which areas","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#role-access","k":"Area Owner Manager Cashier Stock keeper Pharmacist Accountant Register: checkout, returns, shift ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ Register: receiving, price check ✓ ✓ price check ✓ ✓ Admin: dashboard ✓ ✓ (branch) ✓ Admin: catalog & pricing ✓ ✓ c"},{"t":"How screens map to code","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#code-structure","k":"apps/admin/src/routes/ (TanStack Router, file-based) ├─ _auth/login.tsx A-01 ├─ _auth/mfa.tsx A-02 ├─ _app/index.tsx A-10 Dashboard ├─ _app/catalog/products/index.tsx A-20 ├─ _app/catalog/products/$id.tsx A-21 ├─ _app/ca"},{"t":"Build order by phase","p":"Screens & navigation","u":"ui-screens.html#build-order","k":"Phase Screens P1 Foundation A-01, A-02, A-03, A-05 (basic), A-80, A-81, A-82, A-83, A-90, P-01, R-01, R-02 P2 Catalog & register A-20–A-24, A-30–A-32, A-66, R-05, R-18, R-19, R-20 P3 Receiving & stock A-40–A-45, A-48, R-"}];
